LIB_LOAD("eb",{"eb1":{"challenge":[{"q":"In which American state was E. M. Bounds born?","o":["Missouri","Georgia","Texas","New York"],"why":"In 1835."},{"q":"What was Bounds's job before he became a preacher?","o":["Lawyer","Doctor","Builder","Sailor"],"why":"He argued cases."},{"q":"\"Men ought always to pray, and not to...\"","o":["faint","eat","sing","run"],"why":"Luke 18:1."},{"q":"\"The Church is looking for better methods; God is looking for better...\"","o":["men","music","money","machines"],"why":"Bounds's famous line."},{"q":"What did Tolu try first to grow her group?","o":["Pizza, speakers and smoke machines","Prayer","Fasting","Bible study"],"why":"The crowd left when the pizza ran out."},{"q":"Who had to rebuild the temple?","o":["Zerubbabel","Solomon","Samuel","David"],"why":"By God's Spirit."},{"q":"\"Not by might, nor by power, but by my...\"","o":["spirit","sword","gold","wisdom"],"why":"Zechariah 4:6."},{"q":"Bounds said the Holy Ghost does not anoint plans, but...?","o":["men of prayer","buildings","money","machines"],"why":"People, not plans."},{"q":"Which of Jesse's sons did God choose?","o":["David, the youngest","Eliab, the tallest","The oldest","None"],"why":"The LORD looks on the heart."},{"q":"Where does God shape a leader's heart, according to Bounds?","o":["In prayer","On stage","In meetings","On social media"],"why":"What you are in secret matters."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does the word 'anoint' mean in the Bible?","o":["Pouring oil on someone to show God chose them","Painting a house","Cooking with oil","Washing your hands"],"why":"Also God's Spirit resting on a person."},"choices":[{"title":"New prefect","q":"You've just been chosen as a class leader. You want everyone to respect you.","o":[{"t":"Pray for your class and ask God to make your heart right.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God works through praying people."},{"t":"Be strict and loud so they fear you.","f":"Power isn't in loudness, but in God's Spirit."},{"t":"Try to be everyone's best friend.","f":"Leadership starts in the heart before God."}]},{"title":"Flashy fix","q":"Your club is struggling. Someone suggests a big, expensive event to fix everything.","o":[{"t":"Pray first, then plan wisely together.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Better people before better methods."},{"t":"Spend everything on the event.","f":"Methods alone don't last when the pizza runs out."},{"t":"Give up on the club.","f":"Pray, and let God work on the leaders first."}]},{"title":"Too big","q":"You've been asked to lead a project that feels impossible.","o":[{"t":"Pray, rely on God's Spirit, and take it one step at a time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Not by might, nor by power, but by My Spirit."},{"t":"Refuse because you're not strong enough.","f":"God's power works through weak people."},{"t":"Pretend you're totally confident.","f":"Real confidence comes from God's Spirit."}]},{"title":"Looking the part","q":"You're choosing a team captain. One person looks impressive; another is quiet but kind and faithful.","o":[{"t":"Look at character, not just appearance.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The LORD looketh on the heart."},{"t":"Pick whoever looks coolest.","f":"Samuel nearly made that mistake!"},{"t":"Pick your best friend.","f":"Choose by character, not favouritism."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of Power Through Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"church","n":"🛠️ God looks for better people, not just better plans."},{"sc":"ruins","n":"🕊️ Not by might, nor by power, but by God's Spirit."},{"sc":"flock","n":"❤️ Leadership starts in the heart."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"⚡ Real power for leaders comes through prayer."}],"stops":{"eb1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"town","n":"In 1835, in the state of Missouri in America, a boy called Edward McKendree Bounds was born. People came to know him as {E. M. Bounds}."},{"sc":"court","n":"He was bright and hard-working. While still a young man, he became a lawyer. He could argue a case brilliantly."},{"sc":"church","n":"But God had other plans. Bounds gave up the law to become a preacher of the gospel. During the American Civil War, he served as a chaplain, caring for soldiers, praying with the wounded and the dying."},{"sc":"church","n":"After the war, he pastored churches and edited a Christian newspaper. Then, for the last years of his life, he lived quietly in a small town in Georgia."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"It's said that there, he rose at four o'clock every morning to pray for three hours before the day began. He prayed for his town, for preachers, for the church around the world."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"I wrote little books about prayer. Not because I was an expert, but because I had seen that nothing in God's work happens without it."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"I wrote mainly for preachers. But you don't need to be a preacher to lead. If you're a prefect, a captain, a big brother or sister, or a youth leader, this is for you."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"shock","t":"I've just been made class prefect! I was going to ask for advice."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Then sit down, young man. Let's talk about real power."}],"quote":{"text":"And he spake a parable unto them to this end, that men ought always to pray, and not to faint.","who":"Luke 18:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A lawyer on his knees","text":"E. M. Bounds was a clever lawyer who became a preacher, a chaplain to soldiers, and a man of prayer, rising early to pray for hours. He wrote to leaders, and that includes young leaders like you."},"think":"Where are you a leader, even in a small way? At home, in class, on a team?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Bounds's first job?","o":["A lawyer","A farmer","A soldier","A teacher"],"why":"He argued cases brilliantly."},{"q":"What did he become during the American Civil War?","o":["A chaplain caring for soldiers","A general","A spy","A cook"],"why":"Praying with the wounded and dying."},{"q":"At what time is he said to have risen to pray?","o":["Four o'clock in the morning","Noon","Midnight only","Ten o'clock"],"why":"For three hours."},{"q":"Who did Bounds mainly write for?","o":["Preachers, and all who lead","Only children","Only lawyers","Only soldiers"],"why":"Young leaders too!"},{"q":"What had Femi just been made?","o":["Class prefect","Football captain","Head of the choir","A lawyer"],"why":"And he wanted advice."}]},"eb1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"Tolu was the new leader of her church's teen group. Only five people came on Fridays, and they looked bored."},{"sc":"church","w":"ebtolu","e":"big","t":"We need a new {method}! Bigger speakers! Smoke machines! Free pizza! A new logo! Then everyone will come!"},{"sc":"church","n":"They tried it all. For two weeks, crowds came for the pizza. Then the pizza ran out, and so did the crowd."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Tolu, I wrote a line about this more than a hundred years ago. The church is looking for better methods; God is looking for better men."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Pizza isn't wrong! Good plans are useful. But God's main plan isn't a programme. It's a person: a leader who walks closely with Him. When the leader changes, everything around them starts to change."},{"sc":"church","w":"ebtolu","e":"worried","t":"So before I plan the next event... I should pray?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Before, during and after! Let God work on you first. Then your plans will have life in them."},{"sc":"church","n":"Tolu began meeting two friends to pray for the group every Wednesday. Slowly, the Friday meetings changed. Fewer gimmicks. More honest talk. And people kept coming back."}],"quote":{"text":"The Church is looking for better methods; God is looking for better men.","who":"Power Through Prayer, Chapter 1","tag":"Bounds's words"},"lesson":{"title":"God works through people","text":"Tolu tried flashy methods, but the crowd left when the pizza ran out. Bounds said: the church looks for better methods; God looks for better people. Plans are useful, but God's main plan is a leader who walks closely with Him."},"think":"Before you plan your next project or event, how could you pray first?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Tolu want at first?","o":["Bigger speakers, smoke machines and pizza","More prayer","Fewer people","A quieter room"],"why":"A new method!"},{"q":"What happened when the pizza ran out?","o":["The crowd left","More came","Nothing changed","They bought more"],"why":"Methods alone didn't last."},{"q":"What did Bounds say God is looking for?","o":["Better men (people)","Better methods","Bigger buildings","More money"],"why":"The church looks for methods."},{"q":"What did Tolu start doing every Wednesday?","o":["Praying with two friends for the group","Buying pizza","Making posters","Sleeping"],"why":"And the group changed."},{"q":"1 Timothy 4:16 says take heed first unto...?","o":["Thyself","Thy money","Thy plans","Thy friends"],"why":"Then the doctrine."}]},"eb1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"ruins","n":"Long ago, God's people came back to Jerusalem after many years in exile. Their temple lay in ruins. Their leader, Zerubbabel, was supposed to rebuild it."},{"sc":"ruins","w":"ebzerub","e":"worried","t":"We're so few. We have so little money. Our enemies keep stopping us. This job is like a mountain!"},{"sc":"ruins","n":"Then God sent a message through the prophet Zechariah."},{"sc":"ruins","n":"'Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts. Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain.'"},{"sc":"ruins","n":"Zerubbabel didn't get a bigger army or more money. But he finished the temple, by God's Spirit."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"That's my point exactly! I wrote: the Holy Ghost does not flow through methods, but through men. He does not come on machinery, but on men. He does not {anoint} plans, but men: men of prayer."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"smile","t":"So as a prefect, my power isn't my badge, or being loud, or being popular. It's God's Spirit working through me."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"And the pipe that the Spirit flows through is prayer."}],"quote":{"text":"The Holy Ghost does not flow through methods, but through men. He does not come on machinery, but on men. He does not anoint plans, but men — men of prayer.","who":"Power Through Prayer, Chapter 1","tag":"Bounds's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Power from the Spirit","text":"Zerubbabel faced a mountain of a job with little strength or money. God said: not by might, nor by power, but by My Spirit. Bounds wrote that the Spirit flows through praying people, not machinery. Your real power as a leader is God's Spirit."},"think":"What 'mountain' are you facing? How would it change things to rely on God's Spirit instead of your own strength?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Zerubbabel have to rebuild?","o":["The temple","A wall","A ship","A palace"],"why":"In Jerusalem, after the exile."},{"q":"What did Zerubbabel's job feel like?","o":["A mountain","A holiday","A game","A feast"],"why":"\"Who art thou, O great mountain?\""},{"q":"Complete: \"Not by might, nor by power, but by my...\"","o":["spirit","army","money","plans"],"why":"Zechariah 4:6."},{"q":"According to Bounds, what does the Holy Ghost flow through?","o":["Men (people) of prayer","Methods","Machinery","Plans"],"why":"He anoints people, not plans."},{"q":"What did Femi realise his real power as a prefect was?","o":["God's Spirit working through him","His badge","Being loud","Being popular"],"why":"And prayer is the pipe."}]},"eb1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","n":"God sent the prophet Samuel to the house of Jesse in Bethlehem to anoint a new king. One by one, Jesse's sons walked past."},{"sc":"farm","n":"First came Eliab: tall, strong and handsome. Samuel was sure."},{"sc":"farm","w":"ebsamuel","e":"smile","t":"Surely the LORD's anointed is before him."},{"sc":"farm","n":"But God said to Samuel: 'Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature... for the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.'"},{"sc":"flock","n":"Seven sons passed, and God chose none of them. Finally, they called the youngest, David, from looking after the sheep. And God said, 'Arise, anoint him: for this is he.'"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"I always said the whole person is behind the sermon. A leader's words only carry the weight of the life behind them. What you are in secret is what you'll give to others."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"worried","t":"So being a good prefect starts with my heart, not with how I look in front of the class."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Yes! And the place where God shapes your heart is in prayer."}],"quote":{"text":"For the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.","who":"1 Samuel 16:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Leadership starts in the heart","text":"Samuel nearly chose the tallest son, but God chose David, because God looks at the heart. Bounds taught that a leader's words carry only the weight of the life behind them. God shapes that heart in prayer."},"think":"If people could see your heart, not just your outside, what would they see? What would you ask God to change?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did God send Samuel?","o":["To Jesse's house in Bethlehem","To Egypt","To Babylon","To Rome"],"why":"To anoint a new king."},{"q":"Which son did Samuel first think was God's choice?","o":["Eliab, the tall one","David","Jesse","Saul"],"why":"But God said no."},{"q":"What does God look on?","o":["The heart","Height","Looks","Clothes"],"why":"1 Samuel 16:7."},{"q":"Where was David when they called him?","o":["Looking after the sheep","At school","At the palace","In the temple"],"why":"The youngest son."},{"q":"What did Bounds say is behind every sermon?","o":["The whole person","Nothing","A microphone","Money"],"why":"Words carry the weight of the life behind them."}]}}},"eb2":{"challenge":[{"q":"Bounds: those who have done the most for God have been early on their...","o":["knees","phones","feet","beds"],"why":"Meet God first."},{"q":"\"My voice shalt thou hear in the...\"","o":["morning","evening","market","night only"],"why":"Psalm 5:3."},{"q":"What did Jesus do the morning after His busy day?","o":["Rose before dawn to pray","Slept in","Went fishing","Had a feast"],"why":"Mark 1:35."},{"q":"Who said \"All men seek for thee\"?","o":["Simon Peter and the disciples","The Pharisees","Herod","Daniel"],"why":"They searched for Jesus."},{"q":"How long did Luther say he needed to pray daily?","o":["Three hours","Three minutes","Three days","No time"],"why":"Because he was so busy."},{"q":"Who was a young missionary who prayed in the woods?","o":["David Brainerd","Martin Luther","Daniel","Zerubbabel"],"why":"He died aged 29."},{"q":"\"O God, thou art my God; ___ will I seek thee.\"","o":["early","later","never","maybe"],"why":"Psalm 63:1."},{"q":"Which king was tricked into making the anti-prayer law?","o":["Darius","David","Herod","Pharaoh"],"why":"Daniel 6."},{"q":"How many times a day did Daniel pray?","o":["Three","Two","Ten","One"],"why":"As he did aforetime."},{"q":"What did God shut in the lions' den?","o":["The lions' mouths","The door","Daniel's eyes","The window"],"why":"Daniel 6:22."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What did Luther say to have prayed well is?","o":["To have studied well","To have slept well","To have eaten well","To have played well"],"why":"Prayer made his time fruitful."},"choices":[{"title":"Snooze button","q":"Your alarm goes off. You could snooze, or get up and spend ten minutes with God.","o":[{"t":"Get up and give God the first ten minutes.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Early on your knees sets the tune for the day."},{"t":"Snooze three times.","f":"Then the rush steals your morning."},{"t":"Check your phone in bed first.","f":"Let God's voice be the first you hear."}]},{"title":"After the big day","q":"You had an amazing day: you won an award. Next morning, you feel like skipping prayer.","o":[{"t":"Thank God and seek Him first, like Jesus after His big day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Even Jesus rose early to pray after His busiest day."},{"t":"Skip it. You're doing great anyway.","f":"Success is a time to stay close to God."},{"t":"Pray only when things go wrong.","f":"Pray in good days and bad."}]},{"title":"Too busy","q":"Exams, chores and practice. You tell yourself you're too busy to pray this week.","o":[{"t":"Pray even more, because you're busy.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Luther prayed more because he had more to do."},{"t":"Pray after exams.","f":"Too busy to pray is the best reason to pray."},{"t":"Skip prayer and sleep more.","f":"Rest is good, but don't skip time with God."}]},{"title":"Mocked for praying","q":"Classmates make fun of you for praying before lunch.","o":[{"t":"Keep praying calmly, as you always have.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Daniel, as he did aforetime."},{"t":"Stop praying in public.","f":"Daniel kept his window open."},{"t":"Pray loudly to show off.","f":"Don't show off; just stay faithful."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"dawn","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of Power Through Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"🌅 Meet God first, before anyone else."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"⛰️ Even Jesus rose early to pray."},{"sc":"study","n":"🕯️ Too busy to pray? That's the best reason to pray."},{"sc":"persia","n":"🪟 Build a prayer habit now. It'll hold you later."}],"stops":{"eb2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Femi's mornings went like this: alarm, snooze, snooze, panic, rush, no breakfast, run for the bus. By 8 o'clock, he already felt behind."},{"sc":"home","w":"ebfemi","e":"worried","t":"I never have time to pray in the morning. I'll do it later."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Femi, I noticed something about the people who did the most for God. I wrote: the men who have done the most for God in this world have been early on their knees."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"When you meet God first, before your phone, before the news, before everyone else's voices, you set the tune for the whole day."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"ebfemi","e":"worried","t":"But I'm not a morning person!"},{"sc":"dawn","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Then start small. You don't need three hours. Go to bed a little earlier. Wake ten minutes earlier. Read a few verses and talk to God before you check anything else."},{"sc":"home","n":"Femi tried it for a week. He was still sleepy. But he noticed his days felt calmer, and he was kinder to his little brother on the way to the bus."}],"quote":{"text":"The men who have done the most for God in this world have been early on their knees.","who":"Power Through Prayer","tag":"Bounds's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Meet God first","text":"Bounds noticed that those who did most for God met Him early. Meeting God first, before your phone and everyone else's voices, sets the tune for your whole day. Start small: ten minutes before anything else."},"think":"What's the first thing you usually look at when you wake up? Could you give those first minutes to God?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Femi's mornings usually go?","o":["Snooze, panic, rush","Calm and peaceful","Early and prayerful","He didn't wake up"],"why":"He felt behind by 8 o'clock."},{"q":"What did Bounds notice about those who did most for God?","o":["They were early on their knees","They slept late","They were rich","They were famous"],"why":"They met God first."},{"q":"What does meeting God first do, according to Bounds?","o":["Sets the tune for the whole day","Nothing","Makes you late","Makes you tired"],"why":"Before other voices."},{"q":"How did Bounds suggest Femi start?","o":["Small: ten minutes earlier","Three hours at once","Never sleep","Skip school"],"why":"Start small."},{"q":"According to Psalm 5:3, when will God hear my voice?","o":["In the morning","Only at night","Never","At lunchtime"],"why":"And I will look up."}]},"eb2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"In the town of Capernaum, Jesus had a huge day. He taught in the synagogue. He healed Peter's mother-in-law. As the sun set, the whole town crowded around the door, and He healed many who were sick."},{"sc":"night","n":"It must have been very late when He finally went to bed. Surely He'd sleep in the next morning?"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"But the Bible says: 'And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed.'"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"ebpeter","e":"worried","t":"Master! We've been looking everywhere for You! All men seek for thee!"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"ebjesus","e":"smile","t":"Let us go into the next towns, that I may preach there also: for therefore came I forth."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Do you see? Jesus, the Son of God, needed that time alone with His Father. And in prayer, He knew exactly what to do next, even when the crowds wanted something else."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"If Jesus rose early to pray after His busiest day, how much more do we need to?"}],"quote":{"text":"And Simon and they that were with him followed after him. And when they had found him, they said unto him, All men seek for thee.","who":"Mark 1:36-37","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Even Jesus prayed first","text":"After a huge day of healing, Jesus rose a great while before dawn to pray alone. When the disciples found Him, He knew exactly where to go next. If Jesus needed time with His Father, how much more do we?"},"think":"After a busy or exciting day, do you rest in God or just rush on? What could you learn from Jesus here?","quiz":[{"q":"In which town did Jesus have a huge day of healing?","o":["Capernaum","Rome","Babylon","Lagos"],"why":"The whole town crowded at the door."},{"q":"Whose mother-in-law did Jesus heal?","o":["Peter's","John's","Mary's","Paul's"],"why":"Mark 1:30-31."},{"q":"When did Jesus get up to pray the next morning?","o":["A great while before day","At lunchtime","He slept in","At sunset"],"why":"Mark 1:35."},{"q":"What did the disciples say when they found Him?","o":["\"All men seek for thee\"","\"Let's go home\"","\"We're hungry\"","\"Where's the boat?\""],"why":"Mark 1:37."},{"q":"What did Jesus know after praying?","o":["Exactly where to go next","Nothing","That He should stay","That He was tired"],"why":"To preach in the next towns."}]},"eb2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"In my book, I told the stories of great leaders who prayed. Let me introduce a few."},{"sc":"study","n":"{Martin Luther} was a busy man. He was writing, teaching and standing up to kings and emperors. People expected him to have no time to pray."},{"sc":"study","w":"ebluther","e":"big","t":"I have so much business that I cannot get on without spending three hours daily in prayer!"},{"sc":"study","n":"Luther also liked to say that to have prayed well is to have studied well. Prayer didn't steal his time; it made his time fruitful."},{"sc":"road","n":"{John Wesley} rode thousands of miles on horseback across Britain preaching. Bounds wrote that he spent two hours a day in prayer, and often began very early in the morning."},{"sc":"woods","n":"{David Brainerd} was a young missionary to Native American peoples. He often went into the woods to pray, sometimes in the cold and snow, for the people he served. He died aged just 29, in the home of Jonathan Edwards, who published his diary. It has inspired missionaries ever since."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Busy? Yes. Too busy to pray? Never. In fact, the busier they were, the more they knew they needed to pray."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebtolu","e":"smile","t":"So 'I'm too busy to pray' is actually the best reason TO pray!"}],"quote":{"text":"I have so much business I cannot get on without spending three hours daily in prayer.","who":"Martin Luther, quoted in Power Through Prayer","tag":"Luther's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Too busy not to pray","text":"Luther, Wesley and Brainerd were some of the busiest people in history. But they prayed for hours, because they knew they couldn't do their work without God. 'Too busy to pray' is really the best reason to pray."},"think":"When are you busiest? How could you make sure prayer comes first then, not last?","quiz":[{"q":"How many hours a day did Luther say he needed to pray?","o":["Three","None","Ten","One minute"],"why":"Because he was so busy!"},{"q":"What did Luther say about praying well?","o":["To have prayed well is to have studied well","It wastes time","It's only for monks","It's boring"],"why":"Prayer made his time fruitful."},{"q":"How did John Wesley travel to preach?","o":["On horseback","By plane","By car","On foot only"],"why":"Thousands of miles across Britain."},{"q":"Where did David Brainerd often go to pray?","o":["Into the woods","To a palace","To a market","To a ship"],"why":"Sometimes in the snow."},{"q":"In whose home did Brainerd die?","o":["Jonathan Edwards's","Luther's","Wesley's","Bounds's"],"why":"Edwards published his diary."}]},"eb2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"persia","n":"Daniel was one of the top leaders in the whole Persian empire. Other leaders were jealous and wanted to get rid of him. But they couldn't find anything wrong with him."},{"sc":"persia","n":"So they tricked King Darius into making a law: for thirty days, anyone who prayed to any god or man except the king would be thrown to the lions."},{"sc":"persia","n":"Daniel heard about the law. He went home, to his upstairs room with its windows open towards Jerusalem."},{"sc":"persia","n":"There he knelt down, three times a day, and prayed and gave thanks to his God, just as he always had. He didn't hide, and he didn't stop."},{"sc":"persia","w":"ebdaniel","e":"smile","t":"The king may change his laws, but my God has not changed. I will pray as I always have."},{"sc":"lionsden","n":"His enemies caught him and he was thrown into the lions' den. But God sent His angel and shut the lions' mouths! In the morning, Daniel came out without a scratch."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Notice: Daniel's prayer wasn't a sudden emergency prayer. It was a habit, three times a day, built over years. So when the crisis came, he didn't panic. He just kept doing what he'd always done."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Build the habit now, in the easy days. Then it will hold you in the hard ones."}],"quote":{"text":"My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions' mouths, that they have not hurt me.","who":"Daniel 6:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Build the habit before the crisis","text":"Daniel prayed three times a day, every day, for years. So when the law against prayer came, he didn't panic. He simply kept praying, and God shut the lions' mouths. Build your prayer habit in the easy days, and it'll hold you in the hard ones."},"think":"What regular times in your day could become your 'open window' prayer times?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did the other leaders want to get rid of Daniel?","o":["They were jealous","He was lazy","He was dishonest","He was rude"],"why":"They found nothing wrong with him."},{"q":"What did the new law forbid?","o":["Praying to anyone except the king","Eating","Singing","Travelling"],"why":"For thirty days."},{"q":"How many times a day did Daniel pray?","o":["Three","One","Seven","None"],"why":"As he did aforetime."},{"q":"Which way did Daniel's windows face?","o":["Towards Jerusalem","Towards Babylon","Towards the sea","Towards the desert"],"why":"Daniel 6:10."},{"q":"What did God do in the lions' den?","o":["Shut the lions' mouths","Made the lions disappear","Let Daniel escape early","Nothing"],"why":"Daniel 6:22."}]}}},"eb3":{"challenge":[{"q":"\"Talking to men for God is a great thing, but talking to God for men is...\"","o":["greater still","a waste","boring","impossible"],"why":"Bounds's words."},{"q":"What did Samuel say would be a sin?","o":["Ceasing to pray for the people","Praying too much","Teaching them","Warning them"],"why":"1 Samuel 12:23."},{"q":"How did Femi pray for his class?","o":["Name by name from the class list","All at once in one word","He didn't","Only for his friends"],"why":"One by one."},{"q":"Who 'laboured fervently' in prayer for the Colossians?","o":["Epaphras","Peter","Stephen","Samuel"],"why":"Colossians 4:12."},{"q":"What does 'intercession' mean?","o":["Praying for other people","A break at school","A song","A meal"],"why":"Carrying others to God."},{"q":"How long did Jesus pray before choosing the twelve?","o":["All night","One minute","A week","A year"],"why":"Luke 6:12."},{"q":"How many apostles did Jesus choose?","o":["Twelve","Ten","Seven","Seventy"],"why":"Luke 6:13."},{"q":"Who were the seven chosen to care for?","o":["Widows","Soldiers","Kings","Fishermen"],"why":"Acts 6."},{"q":"Acts 6:4: we will give ourselves continually to...?","o":["prayer and the ministry of the word","cooking","travel","rest"],"why":"First things first."},{"q":"What did Femi realise was stealing his prayer time?","o":["Doing everything himself","Sleeping","His friends","Football"],"why":"Share the work!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! In the Yoruba proverb, what does a honey-seeker want?","o":["The honey inside a rock","The axe","The bees","The tree"],"why":"And doesn't fear the axe's edge."},"choices":[{"title":"Nagging","q":"Your little brother keeps misbehaving. You've told him off a hundred times.","o":[{"t":"Keep guiding him kindly, and start praying for him every day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Talking to God for people is greater still."},{"t":"Shout louder.","f":"Try talking to God about him too."},{"t":"Give up on him.","f":"Samuel never stopped praying for his people."}]},{"title":"Quick prayers","q":"Your friend's parents are sick, and your prayers for her are always rushed.","o":[{"t":"Set aside real time to pray earnestly for her family.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Labour fervently, like Epaphras."},{"t":"Keep praying in five seconds.","f":"Real intercession takes effort and love."},{"t":"Stop praying because it's hard.","f":"The honey is worth the axe."}]},{"title":"Big choice","q":"You need to choose which secondary school subjects to take. It feels huge.","o":[{"t":"Pray about it for days, and ask wise adults for advice.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Big decisions deserve big prayer."},{"t":"Pick what your friends pick.","f":"Seek God first."},{"t":"Choose at random.","f":"Jesus prayed all night before His big choice."}]},{"title":"Too much to do","q":"You're leading a project and doing every job yourself. You've stopped praying.","o":[{"t":"Share tasks with others, and put prayer back at the top.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! First things first, like the apostles."},{"t":"Keep doing it all alone.","f":"That pushes prayer to the bottom."},{"t":"Quit the project.","f":"Share the load, don't drop it."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of Power Through Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"hill","n":"🗣️ Talk to God about the people you lead."},{"sc":"prison","n":"🤼 Pray earnestly. Real prayer is real work."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🌙 Give big decisions big prayer."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"🥇 Share the work, and keep prayer first."}],"stops":{"eb3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"big","t":"As prefect, I've given my class lots of speeches. 'Be quiet! Tidy up! Be kind!' But they still don't listen."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Femi, here's one of my favourite lines: talking to men for God is a great thing, but talking to God for men is greater still."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"You've been talking to your class about God's ways. That's good! But have you been talking to God about your class?"},{"sc":"hill","n":"Long ago, Israel demanded a king. It was a bad choice, and they had rejected God's way. Samuel, their old leader, warned them. They were frightened and begged him to pray for them."},{"sc":"hill","w":"ebsamuel","e":"smile","t":"Fear not... Moreover as for me, God forbid that I should sin against the LORD in ceasing to pray for you: but I will teach you the good and the right way."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Did you hear that? Samuel said that to stop praying for his people would be a sin! For a leader, prayer for your people isn't extra. It's the job."},{"sc":"home","n":"That night, Femi took his class list and prayed for each name, one by one. It took twenty minutes. Some names he'd never prayed for before."},{"sc":"college","n":"Over the next weeks, Femi found himself noticing his classmates more, the quiet ones, the sad ones, the troublemakers. Praying for them made him care about them."}],"quote":{"text":"Talking to men for God is a great thing, but talking to God for men is greater still.","who":"Power Through Prayer","tag":"Bounds's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Talk to God about them","text":"Femi talked to his class about doing right, but hadn't talked to God about his class. Samuel said it would be a sin to stop praying for his people. Bounds says: talking to God for people is even greater than talking to people for God."},"think":"Make a list of people you lead or influence. Pray for each one by name this week.","quiz":[{"q":"What had Femi been doing a lot of?","o":["Giving speeches to his class","Praying for his class","Sleeping","Playing football"],"why":"But they didn't listen."},{"q":"According to Bounds, what is greater than talking to men for God?","o":["Talking to God for men","Talking louder","Writing books","Saying nothing"],"why":"Pray for your people!"},{"q":"What did Samuel say would be a sin?","o":["To stop praying for his people","To pray too much","To talk to the king","To teach them"],"why":"1 Samuel 12:23."},{"q":"What did Femi do with his class list?","o":["Prayed for each name","Threw it away","Gave it to the teacher","Wrote jokes on it"],"why":"One by one."},{"q":"What happened to Femi as he prayed for his class?","o":["He began to care more about them","He got bored","Nothing","He stopped being prefect"],"why":"Prayer grows love."}]},"eb3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"prison","n":"Paul was a prisoner in Rome, chained to a guard. With him was a friend called Epaphras, who had started the church in a town called {Colossae}."},{"sc":"prison","w":"ebepaphras","e":"worried","t":"Lord, keep the believers in Colossae strong. Don't let false teachers lead them astray. Help them stand firm and grow in Your will!"},{"sc":"prison","n":"Day after day, Epaphras prayed for them. Not quick, sleepy prayers, but prayers that took everything he had."},{"sc":"prison","w":"ebpaul","e":"smile","t":"I must tell the Colossians about this when I write to them. Epaphras is always labouring {fervently} for you in prayers."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"The word Paul used for 'labouring' is like an athlete straining in a contest, or a wrestler fighting with all his strength. Real prayer is work!"},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"ebtolu","e":"worried","t":"Work? I thought prayer was supposed to be peaceful and easy."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"It is peaceful, because we rest in God. But {intercession}, carrying other people to God, takes effort. Focus. Time. Love. Like training for a race, it's hard, but it makes you strong."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"ebtolu","e":"smile","t":"My grandmother has a Yoruba saying: if you want the honey inside the rock, you don't look at the edge of the axe."}],"quote":{"text":"Epaphras... always labouring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God.","who":"Colossians 4:12","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Prayer takes effort","text":"Epaphras laboured in prayer for his church like an athlete straining in a race. Bounds says real prayer is work: it takes focus, time and love. But the honey is worth the effort of the axe."},"think":"Who is someone you could 'wrestle' in prayer for, praying earnestly for them every day this week?","proverb":{"text":"Ẹni tí yóò jẹ oyin inú àpáta, kì í wo ẹnu àáké.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Whoever wants to eat the honey inside a rock does not worry about the edge of the axe. Good things are worth hard work."},"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Paul when Epaphras was with him?","o":["In prison in Rome","In Colossae","In Jerusalem","On a ship"],"why":"Chained to a guard."},{"q":"Which church had Epaphras started?","o":["Colossae","Rome","Corinth","Ephesus"],"why":"And he prayed for it."},{"q":"What did Paul say Epaphras was always doing?","o":["Labouring fervently in prayers","Sleeping","Complaining","Travelling"],"why":"Colossians 4:12."},{"q":"What did Bounds compare 'labouring' in prayer to?","o":["An athlete or wrestler straining","Taking a nap","Watching TV","Eating"],"why":"Real prayer is work."},{"q":"According to the Yoruba proverb, what doesn't a honey-seeker worry about?","o":["The edge of the axe","The bees","The rain","The rock"],"why":"Good things are worth the work."}]},"eb3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Tolu had to choose four people to help lead the teen group. Everyone wanted to be picked. Her best friends were expecting it."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebtolu","e":"worried","t":"If I don't choose my friends, they'll be upset. But are they really the right people?"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Jesus once had an even bigger choice. He had many followers. Now He had to choose twelve to be His apostles, who would carry His message to the world."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"The Bible says: 'He went out into a mountain to pray, and continued all night in prayer to God. And when it was day, he called unto him his disciples: and of them he chose twelve.'"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"ebjesus","e":"smile","t":"Ye have not chosen me, but I have chosen you, and ordained you, that ye should go and bring forth fruit."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"The Son of God prayed all night before a big decision! If He needed to, how much more do we, before choosing friends, a team, a school, or a future?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"Tolu didn't pray all night. But she prayed every evening for a week, and asked her youth pastor for advice."},{"sc":"college","n":"She chose two of her friends, and two quiet people she'd hardly noticed before: faithful, kind and dependable. The team turned out to be the best the group had ever had."}],"quote":{"text":"And when it was day, he called unto him his disciples: and of them he chose twelve, whom also he named apostles.","who":"Luke 6:13","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pray before big decisions","text":"Before choosing His twelve apostles, Jesus prayed all night. Tolu prayed for a week before choosing her team, and God led her to faithful people she'd hardly noticed. Big decisions deserve big prayer."},"think":"What big decision is coming up in your life? How could you give it extra time in prayer?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Tolu have to choose?","o":["Four people to help lead the group","A new dress","A song","A school"],"why":"Everyone wanted to be picked."},{"q":"What did Jesus do before choosing the twelve?","o":["Prayed all night on a mountain","Held a vote","Asked the crowd","Picked randomly"],"why":"Luke 6:12."},{"q":"How many apostles did Jesus choose?","o":["Twelve","Seven","Seventy","Three"],"why":"Luke 6:13."},{"q":"What else did Tolu do besides praying?","o":["Asked her youth pastor for advice","Flipped a coin","Asked her phone","Nothing"],"why":"Prayer and wise counsel."},{"q":"Who did Tolu choose?","o":["Two friends and two faithful quiet people","Only her best friends","Nobody","The most popular kids"],"why":"The best team ever!"}]},"eb3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The church in Jerusalem was growing fast. Thousands of new believers! But a problem came up. Some widows were being missed when food was handed out each day, and people were complaining."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The apostles could have dropped everything and run the food programme themselves. It was important work. But they knew what God had called them to do first."},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"ebpeter","e":"smile","t":"Look ye out among you seven men of honest report, full of the Holy Ghost and wisdom, whom we may appoint over this business. But we will give ourselves continually to prayer, and to the ministry of the word."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"So the church chose seven faithful men, including Stephen, to look after the widows. The widows were cared for. The apostles kept praying and preaching. And the word of God spread even more!"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Leaders always have a hundred urgent things shouting for attention. The danger is that prayer gets pushed to the bottom of the list. The apostles put it at the top."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"worried","t":"I've been doing everything myself as prefect. No wonder I never have time to pray!"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Share the work. Trust others. And guard your prayer time like treasure. It's the engine that drives everything else."}],"quote":{"text":"But we will give ourselves continually to prayer, and to the ministry of the word.","who":"Acts 6:4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Guard your prayer time","text":"When the Jerusalem church faced a crisis, the apostles chose others to help, so they could keep prayer and God's word first. Bounds warns that prayer easily slips to the bottom of a leader's list. Share the work, and guard your prayer time like treasure."},"think":"What's pushing prayer to the bottom of your list? What could you share or let go of?","quiz":[{"q":"What problem came up in the Jerusalem church?","o":["Some widows were missed when food was handed out","There was no money","Everyone left","The building fell down"],"why":"Acts 6:1."},{"q":"How many men were chosen to help?","o":["Seven","Twelve","Three","Forty"],"why":"Full of the Holy Ghost and wisdom."},{"q":"Which famous believer was one of the seven?","o":["Stephen","Paul","Daniel","Samuel"],"why":"Acts 6:5."},{"q":"What did the apostles give themselves to continually?","o":["Prayer and the ministry of the word","Cooking","Building","Travel"],"why":"Acts 6:4."},{"q":"What did Bounds call prayer time?","o":["The engine that drives everything else","Optional","A waste of time","Only for Sundays"],"why":"Guard it like treasure."}]}}},"eb4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Philippians 1:3: I thank my God upon every ___ of you.","o":["remembrance","letter","visit","gift"],"why":"Paul prayed with joy."},{"q":"What did Bounds say a true leader carries to God?","o":["His people","His money","His trophies","His plans only"],"why":"Pray for those you lead."},{"q":"What did Tolu brush off after her talk?","o":["A crying younger girl","A phone call","Her friends","Her pastor"],"why":"A full head, an empty heart."},{"q":"\"Create in me a clean ___, O God.\"","o":["heart","house","page","room"],"why":"Psalm 51:10."},{"q":"What does 'contrite' mean?","o":["Truly sorry","Very clever","Very loud","Very fast"],"why":"A broken and contrite heart."},{"q":"What must never go out, according to Leviticus 6:13?","o":["The fire on the altar","The lamp in the house","The stars","The sun"],"why":"Add wood every morning."},{"q":"What is your 'fresh wood', according to Bounds?","o":["Daily prayer and Bible reading","Camp feelings","Big events","Loud music"],"why":"Never let it go out."},{"q":"How many times did Elijah send his servant to look?","o":["Seven","Two","Ten","Forty"],"why":"Then a little cloud."},{"q":"\"The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth...\"","o":["much","nothing","a little","sometimes"],"why":"James 5:16."},{"q":"In what year did E. M. Bounds die?","o":["1913","1835","1950","1800"],"why":"Many books were published after his death."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What was the little cloud Elijah's servant saw compared to?","o":["A man's hand","A sheep","A loaf of bread","A bird"],"why":"1 Kings 18:44."},"choices":[{"title":"Captain's job","q":"You're captain of your school team. Before the big match, you could do a pep talk, or pray for your team too.","o":[{"t":"Encourage them, and pray for each teammate by name.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Real leaders carry their people to God."},{"t":"Just shout motivational words.","f":"Talking to God for people is greater still."},{"t":"Only think about your own performance.","f":"A leader cares for the whole team."}]},{"title":"After the applause","q":"Everyone praises your performance, but a friend who struggled looks upset.","o":[{"t":"Leave the praise and go and encourage your friend.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Keep a soft heart, not just a clever head."},{"t":"Enjoy the praise; they'll be fine.","f":"That's a full head with an empty heart."},{"t":"Tell them to cheer up.","f":"Sit with them and listen."}]},{"title":"Post-camp slump","q":"You felt close to God at a conference, but now you've stopped praying.","o":[{"t":"Start again tomorrow with ten minutes of prayer and Bible.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Add fresh wood every morning."},{"t":"Wait for the next big event.","f":"A fire needs daily wood, not yearly bonfires."},{"t":"Decide the feeling was fake.","f":"Feelings fade; faithfulness keeps the fire going."}]},{"title":"Nothing happening","q":"You've prayed six times for something and seen nothing yet.","o":[{"t":"Keep praying and watch for the little cloud.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Elijah prayed seven times."},{"t":"Give up now.","f":"The answer might be one prayer away."},{"t":"Get angry with God.","f":"Tell Him honestly how you feel, and keep trusting."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"prison","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Power Through Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"prison","n":"🫶 Pray for the people you lead, by name and with joy."},{"sc":"palace","n":"💧 Keep your heart soft, not just your head full."},{"sc":"altar","n":"🔥 Add fresh wood every morning. Never let the fire go out."},{"sc":"carmel","n":"🌧️ Ordinary people can pray powerful prayers. Keep praying!"}],"stops":{"eb4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"prison","n":"Paul was in prison again, in chains. He had every reason to think only about himself. Instead, he picked up his pen and wrote to his friends in the church at Philippi."},{"sc":"prison","w":"ebpaul","e":"smile","t":"I thank my God upon every remembrance of you, always in every prayer of mine for you all making request with joy."},{"sc":"prison","n":"Paul's letters are full of prayers for the people he led: for the Romans, the Ephesians, the Colossians, the Thessalonians, for Timothy and Philemon. He carried them all in his heart."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"A true leader doesn't just give orders. He carries his people to God. A captain who never prays for his team, or a prefect who never prays for his class, is missing the most powerful thing he can do."},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"smile","t":"My dad says something in Yoruba: an elder doesn't stay in the market while the baby's head hangs crooked on its mother's back."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Ha! Yes. Leaders notice and care for those in their charge. And one of the best ways to care is to pray."},{"sc":"college","n":"Femi wrote a short note to his class at the end of term: 'I've prayed for each of you by name this term. Thank you for a great year.' Several classmates kept the note for years."}],"quote":{"text":"I thank my God upon every remembrance of you, always in every prayer of mine for you all making request with joy.","who":"Philippians 1:3-4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Carry your people to God","text":"Even in prison, Paul prayed with joy for every church he led. Bounds says real leaders don't just give orders; they carry their people to God. One of the best ways to care for those you lead is to pray for them."},"think":"Who has God put in your care: siblings, teammates, younger children at church? Pray for them by name today.","proverb":{"text":"Àgbà kì í wà lọ́jà kí orí ọmọ títún wọ́.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"An elder does not stay in the market and let a baby's head hang crooked on its mother's back. Those in charge must notice and care for the people around them."},"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Paul when he wrote to the Philippians?","o":["In prison","On holiday","In a palace","At home"],"why":"In chains."},{"q":"How did Paul pray for the Philippians?","o":["With joy","Angrily","Rarely","He didn't"],"why":"Philippians 1:4."},{"q":"What did Bounds say a true leader does?","o":["Carries his people to God","Just gives orders","Ignores people","Only gives speeches"],"why":"Prayer is the most powerful thing."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb say an elder doesn't do?","o":["Let a baby's head hang crooked in the market","Go to market","Buy food","Carry babies"],"why":"Leaders notice and care."},{"q":"What did Femi write in his note to his class?","o":["That he'd prayed for each of them by name","A list of rules","A complaint","A joke"],"why":"They kept it for years."}]},"eb4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"Tolu gave a brilliant talk at youth group. Clever points, great jokes, perfect slides. Everyone clapped."},{"sc":"church","n":"But afterwards, when a younger girl came up crying and wanted to talk, Tolu brushed her off. She was busy enjoying the compliments."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"worried","t":"Tolu, I wrote a lot about this. A leader can have a full head and an empty heart. Clever words without a loving heart are like a lamp with no oil."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"The heart is learned in the school of prayer. When we kneel before God, honestly, He breaks our pride and fills us with His love for people."},{"sc":"palace","n":"King David once did something very wrong. He tried to cover it up, and hurt people badly. Then God sent the prophet Nathan to help him see what he'd done."},{"sc":"palace","w":"ebdavid","e":"worried","t":"Have mercy upon me, O God... Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me."},{"sc":"palace","n":"David didn't make excuses. He came to God with a broken, {contrite} heart. And God forgave him."},{"sc":"church","w":"ebtolu","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I was proud. I'm sorry. Give me a soft heart for people like that girl."},{"sc":"church","n":"The next week, Tolu found the younger girl and sat with her for an hour, just listening. It mattered more than any talk she'd ever given."}],"quote":{"text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.","who":"Psalm 51:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Head and heart","text":"Tolu's talk was brilliant, but her heart wasn't soft towards a hurting girl. Bounds warned that a leader can have a full head and an empty heart. Prayer is where God softens our hearts, like David, who came to God broken and was made new."},"think":"Is your heart soft towards the people you lead? Ask God to create a clean heart in you today.","quiz":[{"q":"What did Tolu do after her brilliant talk?","o":["Brushed off a crying younger girl","Hugged everyone","Went home","Prayed for everyone"],"why":"She was enjoying compliments."},{"q":"What did Bounds compare clever words without love to?","o":["A lamp with no oil","A full cup","A strong wall","A sunny day"],"why":"A full head, an empty heart."},{"q":"Where did Bounds say the heart is learned?","o":["In the school of prayer","At university","On stage","Online"],"why":"God softens our hearts there."},{"q":"Who helped David see what he had done?","o":["The prophet Nathan","Samuel","Elijah","Daniel"],"why":"And David came to God broken."},{"q":"According to Psalm 51:17, what will God not despise?","o":["A broken and contrite heart","A proud heart","A clever speech","Rich gifts"],"why":"He forgives the truly sorry."}]},"eb4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"At youth camp, Femi felt on fire for God. He prayed every morning, read his Bible every night, and sang at the top of his voice."},{"sc":"home","n":"But three weeks after camp, things had changed. He'd stopped praying in the mornings. His Bible was under a pile of clothes. The fire was almost out."},{"sc":"home","w":"ebfemi","e":"worried","t":"What happened? I felt so close to God at camp."},{"sc":"altar","n":"In the tabernacle long ago, God gave the priests a special command about the fire on the altar."},{"sc":"altar","n":"'The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.' Every morning, the priest added fresh wood to keep it burning."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"Femi, feelings from a camp are like a big flame. Wonderful! But a fire that isn't fed goes out. The priests didn't wait to feel like it. They added wood every single morning."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"Daily prayer is your fresh wood. Daily Bible reading is your fresh wood. It may not always blaze, but it never goes out."},{"sc":"home","n":"Femi dug out his Bible and put it next to his alarm clock. The next morning, he added his first piece of 'wood'. Small, but burning."}],"quote":{"text":"Wherefore I put thee in remembrance that thou stir up the gift of God, which is in thee.","who":"2 Timothy 1:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Add wood every morning","text":"Femi's camp fire faded because he stopped feeding it. God told the priests to keep the altar fire burning by adding wood every morning. Daily prayer and Bible reading are your fresh wood. Not always a blaze, but never out."},"think":"Has your 'fire' for God faded? What fresh wood could you add tomorrow morning?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Femi feel at youth camp?","o":["On fire for God","Bored","Angry","Homesick"],"why":"Praying, reading and singing."},{"q":"Where was Femi's Bible three weeks later?","o":["Under a pile of clothes","In his hands","At church","On the shelf, open"],"why":"The fire was almost out."},{"q":"What did God say about the fire on the altar?","o":["It shall never go out","Let it go out at night","Light it once a year","Use it to cook"],"why":"Leviticus 6:13."},{"q":"What did the priests add every morning?","o":["Fresh wood","Water","Sand","Flowers"],"why":"To keep it burning."},{"q":"Where did Femi put his Bible?","o":["Next to his alarm clock","In the bin","At school","Under the bed"],"why":"His first piece of wood."}]},"eb4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"carmel","n":"For three and a half years there had been no rain in Israel. Then, on top of Mount Carmel, the prophet Elijah bowed down with his face between his knees, and prayed for rain."},{"sc":"carmel","w":"ebelijah","e":"smile","t":"Go up now, look toward the sea."},{"sc":"carmel","w":"ebservant","e":"worried","t":"There is nothing."},{"sc":"carmel","n":"Elijah kept praying. 'Go again,' he said. Seven times the servant went to look. Seven times Elijah prayed."},{"sc":"carmel","w":"ebservant","e":"shock","t":"Behold, there ariseth a little cloud out of the sea, like a man's hand!"},{"sc":"storm","n":"Soon the sky grew black with clouds and wind, and there was a great rain!"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"smile","t":"James tells us that {Elias} was a man subject to like passions as we are. An ordinary person, with feelings and fears like yours! And yet his prayers moved heaven."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"E. M. Bounds kept praying for the rest of his life. In his last years in Georgia, he rose early every morning to pray for hours. He died in 1913, aged 78. Friends gathered up his writings and published many of them after his death."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"bounds","e":"big","t":"So, young leaders: God is looking for better people, not just better plans. Meet Him early. Pray for your people. Keep your heart soft and your fire burning. And never stop praying!"},{"sc":"college","w":"ebfemi","e":"big","t":"Lead on our knees!"},{"sc":"college","w":"ebtolu","e":"big","t":"Every single day!"}],"quote":{"text":"Elias was a man subject to like passions as we are, and he prayed earnestly that it might not rain... And he prayed again, and the heaven gave rain.","who":"James 5:17-18","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Ordinary people, powerful prayers","text":"Elijah was an ordinary person like us, yet he prayed seven times until a small cloud brought a great rain. Bounds spent his life praying, and his little books still light fires. God's power is available to young leaders who pray."},"think":"What are you praying for that seems like 'nothing' is happening yet? Keep going. Look for the little cloud!","quiz":[{"q":"How long had there been no rain in Israel?","o":["Three and a half years","One week","Ten years","One day"],"why":"James 5:17."},{"q":"Where did Elijah pray for rain?","o":["On Mount Carmel","In Jerusalem","In Babylon","In a boat"],"why":"Face between his knees."},{"q":"How many times did the servant go to look?","o":["Seven","Three","Once","Twelve"],"why":"And Elijah kept praying."},{"q":"What did the servant finally see?","o":["A little cloud like a man's hand","A lion","A ship","A rainbow"],"why":"Then a great rain!"},{"q":"What does James say about Elijah?","o":["He was a man like us","He was a superhero","He never had fears","He was an angel"],"why":"Ordinary, yet powerful in prayer."}]}}}});
